# Design / internal docs (kept local)
DESIGN.md
docs/
.docs/
# `.claude/` and `.agents/` hold PERSONAL settings (settings.local.json), local
# agent definitions and hooks -- none of which belong to anybody but their owner.
# Their `skills/` directories are different: the rc-repro skill is a project
# artifact, and committing it is how a fresh clone teaches an agent to drive this
# tool correctly. So the contents are ignored and that one subdirectory is not,
# which needs `dir/*` rather than `dir/` -- git will not descend into an excluded
# directory to re-include something inside it.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
# The rest of `.claude` splits cleanly into project artifacts and personal state.
# `agents/` (the code-reviewer, live-verifier and regression-prover definitions),
# `hooks/guard-commit.py` (which enforces two CLAUDE.md rules that have been broken
# here before) and `settings.json` (which wires that hook) describe how to work on
# THIS repository, so a teammate's clone should have them.
# `settings.local.json` is one person's permission allow-list and stays out.
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.codex/
.agents/*
!.agents/skills/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
